Policy/process for requesting addition to OSF DCE mailing lists
---------------------------------------------------------------

OSF has a number of DCE-related mailing lists that are available
to DCE-interested parties.  In order to request addition to these 
lists, mail should be sent to 

		<maillist>-request@osf.org

Your request should include a mention of who you are, what 
organization you work for, and your email address.

PLEASE NOTE THAT MAIL REQUESTING ADDITION TO A MAILLIST SHOULD NOT 
BE SENT TO THE MAILLIST ITSELF.  This results in everyone on that
list receiving your request, which is not necessary.  

The current externally available DCE maillists that are available
to people interested in DCE, and the policies governing access to 
them, are as follows:

	dce-talk	General DCE discussion mailling list -
			Available to DCE-interested parties in 
			any organization

	sig-dce		DCE Special Interest Group (SIG) maillist
			list - Available to DCE-interested parties 
			at OSF member organizations
			
	sig-dce-<working group name>

			There are many of these lists, one for each
			Working Group (subgroups) of the DCE SIG.
			(ex. sig-dce-business, sig-dce-security,
			sig-dce-fs, etc.)
			As with the sig-dce list, these lists are
			available to OSF member organizations.

Upon receipt of your request and verification of your access to that
list, the person responsible for maintaining the maillist you would 
like to be added to should confirm for you that your request has
been addressed.

Questions about OSF maillists can be addressed to postmaster@osf.org.




