Larry Buickel <larry@austin.ibm.com> wrote:
>What's the real scoop?  Thanks ...

As far as I can tell (from looking at the source) you're limited only
by available virtual memory.

Note that each call execution thread requires a thread stack which
takes typically 32k-64k bytes (depending on your hardware
architecture).

In most servers you probably don't want more than about 10 or 20
executor threads anyhow, because you'll probably spend all your time
competing for locks on shared data structures..

					- Bill


