Canned message follows.

A light, per-component introduction to DCE:
    Introduction to DCE
    Published by Prentice-Hall (ISBN 0-13-490624-1).
    If you cannot get it from your local bookstore,
    call Prentice-Hall at +1 515 284 6751 for individual orders.

A complete set of current DCE documentation (occupies nearly a foot of
shelf space) is available from OSF; contact <direct@osf.org>.  This includes
the manpages, development guides, porting guide, and administration
documentation.  I believe it is also available from Prentice-Hall.

For information on how to write DCE RPC programs:
    Guide to writing DCE applications
    by John Shirley
    Published by O'Reilly and Associates (ISBN 1-56592-004-X).
    If you cannot get it at your local bookstore, call O'Reilly at +1 800
    338 6887 in the US or +1 707 829 0515 for international orders.

Another introduction that many people prefer is:
    Understanding DCE
    Ward Rosenberry, David Kenney, & Gerry Fisher
    Published by O'Reilly and Associates (ISBN: 1-56592-005-8)


