> expense might conceivably be saved under the scenario you have described.

How about not "intentionally keep it totally devoid of native compilers" but
haven't had the time/resources to produce them all yet. It takes time to
write compilers for new architectures.

> The fact is however that this will NEVER happen here in the real world.

Funny I could have sworn I have used machines that didn't support every
know programming language. Obviously I was on another planet at the time.

> Note also that even if this *didn't* happen, it would be pretty damned
