> So, what about more advanced optimizations like loop tiling, vectorization,
> parallelization, etc -- many of these require specific knowledge of cache
> structure, vector hardware, and so forth.  Does ANDF address any of this?

I believe so.  The ANDF representation is supposed to keep enough
high-level information about the program to allow this kind of
optimization to be done by the installer.  Not only does it keep
useful high-level information contained in the original source code,
but it is specifically designed to allow compilers to produce and
record *more* global information.  In that sense, it should be
better than using C as an intermediate language.

