Maybe I missed a major feature of ANDF, but it seems that most portability
problems are due to the poliferation of Unixes, each of which is subtlely
different (and better, of course).  C is universally available, but porting
software is still a major headache becasue every system differs.  Windows NT's
advantage is not that it is a better OS than Unix, but rather its code is 
controlled by a single vendor and will be the same on all platforms.

ANDF may be a reasonable delivery mechanism, but I don't see that it addresses
the really hard problems in writing software that runs on Unix systemS. 

