	the RPC threads package is quite specific
	to the host system's chip architecture. As a result,
	there are some DCE architectural issues that need
	to be solved by the vendors, says Mitre."
Does anyone know what they mean by this?
Does it refer to problems implementing pthreads?
(Mitre apparently did their own port of DCE to the HP 9000/932)
Or are they saying that there are architecture characteristics
