keith@ksmith.com (Keith Smith) writes:

>Basically an installer is a glorified name for an ANDF Compiler, and
>ANDF is simply a Vanilla CPU specification.  How long before you get
>ANDF "MicroCoded" into a RISC core?

I believe ANDF isn't straight-line code, but tree-structured.
Executing tree-structured code at machine-level is not likely to be
fast (though some Forth proponents may disagree).

Even if we flatten the tree, it may not be an advantage to execute the
code directly. It is for example better to compile p-code to RISC code
than microcode/hardwire the p-code directly.

