In article <1993Dec2.082256@cs.utwente.nl>, kremer@cs.utwente.nl (Harro Kremer) writes:
|> 
|> Can someone tell me what ANDF is?
|> 
ANDF stands for Architecture Neutral Distribution Format.  It has been
a research project of the Open Software Foundation since that
organization was founded.

The idea is to convert ISO Standard C into a mostly-compiled format
that can be installed on any system without regard to the instruction
set of the CPU.  The "Installer" reads ANDF and converts it to the
instruction set of the target.

ANDF has been a technical success but a commercial flop.  There is
an ANDF compiler and several very effective installers, however, 
very few software vendors are willing to embrace the technology for
their product.

In the mean time, some new uses are bing found for the ANDF tools.
For example, as tests for standards conformance.

For more information contact the OSF at +1-617-621-8700 or FAX
+1+617-225-2943

