Citibank's Global Finance Technology Division announces the public
distribution of a set of C++ class libraries designed to increase the
ease of use for OSF DCE and Transarc Encina.  The Objdce class library
encapsulates the features of DCE security, naming, threads, and time.
The Objtran class library adds to this transactional capabilities as
implemented by Transarc's Encina.  Finally, the YADDL component(yet
another data definition language) provides a mechanism for easily
defining classes which can be sent as arguments to RPCs, or stored and
retrieved to and from Transarc SFS and RQS files.

Citibank cannot provide software support for these class libraries.  We are
distributing this software for the value it will provide others who
are implementing or planning to implement C++ class libraries for DCE
and/or Encina.  We hope to provide by example input into the design of
these potential offerings.

Prerequisites for the use of Objdce include:

   o A C++ compiler that handles templates. A cfront 3.0.1-based compiler
     is good. We have successfully compiled this software with the Sun
     SparcWorks 2.0.1 compiler under SunOS 4.1.3 and 5.2, on HP-UX with the
     HP C++ compiler, and on AIX 3.2.2 with the IBM version 1.0 "xlC"
     compiler.  Objtran and Objdce may or may not work properly with gcc.
   o DCE version 1.0.1 or 1.0.2. Note that HP DCE 1.1 is equivalent to OSF
     DCE 1.0.2.
   o The USL Standard Components version 3.0. This comes bundled with the
     HP C++ compiler. On other platforms, you must purchase a license from
     USL. For information, contact Jerilyn Beenders: jerilyn@usl.com, or
     908-522-6010. 
   o GNU make. This is available via anonymous FTP from prep.ai.mit.edu
     and ftp.uu.net. You can also purchase a binary copy from Cygnus.

Prerequisites for the use of Objtran and YADDL include:
   o Objdce and its prerequisites
   o Encina version 1.0.3B or higher.
   o GNU flex (YADDL only)
   o GNU yacc (YADDL only)

This software will be provided as source code and includes user
manuals in LaTex and Postscript format and man pages in nroff and
troff format.  At this time, we are unable to provide anonymous ftp
access so if you are interested in receiving a copy of the latest
release send e-mail to objtran-request@fig.citib.com and we will reply
with a uuencoded compressed tar file.  If you are only interested in
the documentation please specify that in your request.  If you are
only interested in the DCE components because you don't have Encina
let us know that also.

