DCE for OpenVMS is being released in a phased approach.  The initial product,
the DCE Developer's Kit for OpenVMS VAX, was released this past summer.
It contained RPC, Threads, and a Local Directory Service as a temporary
stand-in for CDS.  This product is a VAX-only implementation of sufficient
functionality to enable DCE application development with RPC.

The second release, Digital DCE for OpenVMS VAX and AXP V1.1, will contain
the so-called "secure core" DCE services.  These consist of RPC,
Threads (shipped as part of the operating system), DTS (client & server),
CDS (client only), and Security (client only).  This product is currently
in External Field Test Update, and is due to be released in February 1994.

The third release, Digital DCE for OpenVMS VAX and AXP V1.2 will add the
CDS and Security servers, and update the code base to OSF DCE V1.0.3.
This product will be available in late spring/early summer 1994.

